  "rationale": "**Verdict:** The requirement is implemented as stated, and the tests cover its main cases. I read the code and tests supplied in the inputs. I did not run the tests.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `marker_ranges` (src/index.rs ~676–728) finds `{requirements-index}` directives.\n  - It uses `colon_fence` to accept an opening fence of three or more colons.\n  - It accepts a closing fence with at least as many colons. A missing closing fence is an error.\n  - It rejects any non-empty body, with the error \"must have an empty body\".\n  - It skips markers inside protected ranges, such as code fences, and inside `req` or other definition blocks.\n- `IndexPlan::find` (~251–293) scans all chapters. A second directive anywhere in the book, including in the same chapter, returns the error \"a book may contain only one {requirements-index} directive\". With no directive it returns `None`.\n- When a directive is present, `find` plans one detail path per definition. The definitions are the requirements and examples collected in `preprocess_book` from chapters that have paths, with terms excluded. It also checks that no detail path collides with an existing chapter.\n- `populate` (~300–396) replaces the directive range with the evidence table. It appends one detail subchapter per definition as a `sub_item` of the index chapter, with section numbers.\n- The real book uses the feature. `md/requirements-index.md` contains the directive and is listed in `md/SUMMARY.md`.\n\n**Tests**\n- `marker_accepts_long_fences_and_ignores_examples` covers these cases:\n  - a directive inside a code fence is ignored;\n  - a directive inside a `req` example block is ignored;\n  - a four-colon fence is accepted;\n  - a missing closing fence is an error;\n  - a non-empty body is an error;\n  - a longer closing fence (five colons closing a four-colon opener) is accepted.\n- `index_shows_evidence_states_and_links_generated_chapters` runs the full `preprocess_book` path.\n  - The directive is replaced, with no leftover `{requirements-index}` text.\n  - The table has a row for each of five requirements.\n  - Exactly five detail subchapters are created, with correct paths, numbering, and content.\n- `repeated_index_markers_fail_with_a_clear_error` covers the rule that a book may contain at most one directive.\n\n**Gaps:** These are minor.\n- No test uses a closing fence shorter than the opener.\n- No test covers the \"standalone\" aspect in other forms, such as indentation.\n\nNeither is a significant gap, and there are no FIXMEs.",
